 {:id :unix-java
  :title "Unix sockets and datagrams, and signals between processes, at the AOT levels"
  :kind :design
  :why "the AOT runtime is Java forms over the JDK's API: Java has no Unix-domain sockets and its runtime's datagram sockets carry nothing (OT23), and a Java program receives no signal of the OS, so kill of another process and a signal from outside are not seen (OT24); oi has both over Go's syscall. Since OC216 (a)'s rest the compiled level has them through its main's host (HostSys, OCAML-SURVEY.md \"As built: OC216 (a), the rest\"); the light level, a Java forms interpreter in stage 0, has no host to ask"
  :decided "OT23 (a), OT24 (a), the user 2026-11-05; at the compiled level reversed by OC216 (a), the user 2026-11-10"
  :match [#"^fail known unix-java: "]}
