 {:id :gc-and-memory
  :title "the collector: finalisers, weak pointers, ephemerons, Gc.Memprof, the words allocated"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the runtime's values are Java's (Go's once compiled) and its collector Go's: finalisers run once Go's collector finds their values unreachable (OC192 (a), the user 2026-11-09: their order within a collection finalise.c's batches', which values are young OCaml's alone), weak arrays and ephemerons hold their contents strongly, Gc's counters of allocated words stay at zero, Gc.Memprof samples nothing; a program that observes the collector sees none of OCaml's Since OC216 (a) (the user 2026-11-10; OC64's counters and OC68 (b)'s weak part reversed for them): a weak array's or an ephemeron's key with an identity is a weak pointer (Go's weak, jrt's WeakReference) emptied by the collection that finds it unreachable, an ephemeron's data dropped with a dead key at the collections the program asks for, Gc.minor, major, full_major and compact counted as gc_ctrl.c counts them (the compactions too), Gc.Tweak's parameters in Sys.runtime_parameters; left in the class: Gc.Memprof and the words allocated (OC218), an ephemeron's key reachable only from its own data (Go has no ephemerons: the data stays the ephemeron's while it lives), a boxed integer key (no identity) Deferred since OT30 (a) (the user, 2026-11-17; doc/ocaml/DEFERRED-TRIAGE.md, \"Triage of 2026-11-17\"): OCaml's heap accounting (words per allocation site, a simulated minor heap, Gc's statistics, Memprof's sampling and callbacks) is OC218 (a)'s work (the user, 2026-11-10) Since queue 438 (2026-11-19; doc/ocaml/OCAML-SURVEY.md, \"As built: queue 438\"): OC218's heap model at the light level too (a simulated minor heap, promote, dealloc_minor and dealloc_major, callbacks at the allocation, profiles per domain), an int64's or a nativeint's box a weak key, the asked collections' ephemeron cleaning repeated to its fixpoint; left: values kept alive by the light level's interpreted frames (a let's slot reused but not cleared: opaque's lifetime, ephetest's dead data, exception_comballoc's and stop_start_in_callback's deallocations), the native allocation counts with bytecode's Lambda (discard_in_callback), Marshal's and custom blocks' sources, a thread's exit in a callback, an ephemeron's key reachable from its data, the major collector's own work"
  :decided "OC11 (a); OC64, OC68; OC216 (a); OT30 (a), the user 2026-11-17 (OC218 (a)'s work)"
  :match [#"^fail known gc: "]}
